{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 16, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "## Lost (and Found) in Japan\n\nJapan. The land of the rising sun. It lived up to every expectation and then some! Just back from a whirlwind 10-day trip, I'm still processing the sensory overload in the best way possible.\n\nFirst stop: Tokyo. The neon-drenched streets of Shibuya were a dizzying delight. I spent hours wandering through quirky shops in Harajuku, marveling at the organized chaos. Food was incredible – from Michelin-starred ramen to delicious street food takoyaki. \n\nNext, a bullet train whisked me to Kyoto. Ancient temples and serene gardens offered a stark contrast to Tokyo’s energy.  Fushimi Inari Shrine, with its thousands of vibrant red torii gates winding up the mountain, was breathtaking. I even managed a traditional tea ceremony – a truly calming experience.\n\nBeyond the big cities, I explored the charming town of Nara, where friendly deer roam freely in Nara Park. It was pure magic!\n\nThe people were incredibly polite and helpful, even with my limited Japanese.  Navigating the public transport was surprisingly easy.\n\nJapan is a country of beautiful contradictions – ancient traditions seamlessly blended with futuristic technology. It’s a place that challenges your senses and leaves you wanting more.  Definitely a trip I won’t soon forget!  Sayonara for now, Japan!\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "##", "logprob": -1.4305104514278355e-06}, {"token": "▁Lost", "logprob": -0.0012646066024899483}, {"token": "▁(", "logprob": -0.14694757759571075}, {"token": "and", "logprob": -9.536738616588991e-07}, {"token": "▁Found", "logprob": -0.0011703077470883727}, {"token": ")", "logprob": -0.11968507617712021}, {"token": "▁in", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁Japan", "logprob": -0.09020631015300751}, {"token": "\n\n", "logprob": -0.2085941582918167}, {"token": "Japan", "logprob": -0.4077354669570923}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.011469616554677